# Windows installer

NSIS assisted installer is branded desktop-owned packaging: `build/installer.nsh` may contain **only** `customWelcomePage` / `customUnWelcomePage` / `customHeader` (GUI pages) — no MessageBox / Section / RequestExecutionLevel / customInstall, so silent `/S`, overwrite upgrade and the SHA512SUMS updater flow stay intact. `customUnWelcomePage` replaces the template's bare `MUI_UNPAGE_WELCOME`, so it must re-insert that page and re-define `MUI_WELCOMEPAGE_TITLE_3LINES` (MUI2 unsets welcome settings per page; otherwise the un-welcome title's third line clips). Keep `oneClick:false`, directory choose, per-user default path, shortcuts, and artifact `Deepseek-Harness-Desktop-Setup-${version}.exe` (release.yml globs depend on it). Bitmaps are fixed-geometry 24-bit BMPs (sidebar 164×314, header 150×57) regenerated via `npm run installer:assets` from `scripts/render-installer-assets.js`; palette mirrors the **official light tokens** (launcher-aligned): sidebar fill `rgb(249,250,251)`, bg-base white, label primary/secondary/tertiary ink, brand blue `rgb(65,118,230)` as thin accent only, hairline `rgba(0,0,0,.10)`. Sidebar brand stack = whale + product name `Deepseek-Harness-Desktop`; uninstaller = muted grayscale of the same light composition. No near-black `#0b0d12` marketing panel, no `--boot-*` instrument canvas — no second skin. Uninstall must not delete `userData` (dsh-home). `deleteAppDataOnUninstall` / `perMachine` stay unset.

Release acceptance: the windows release job runs `npm run smoke:packaged` on `dist/win-unpacked` between `npm run dist` and the artifact upload — BLOCKING, two in-step attempts, no `continue-on-error`; macOS stays best-effort with no smoke. This is artifact acceptance, not a repeat of test.yml quality gates (`npm test` / `test:gui` stay banned from release.yml). Placement pinned by `ci-isolation.test.js`. Validate via `workflow_dispatch` before tagging.

